        <mxCell id="c208" value="&lt;i&gt;Report view, page Timing, drawn here in a different arrangement (the model answer&#x27;s page also holds a text box with the written answer, not drawn). Blue circles: the rate by the month of the credit, 0.040% in 2024-01, the first month of the first year, which had nothing earlier to return. Amber diamonds: the rate by the month of the shipment, which falls to 0.055% in 2026-12 (outlined in coral, with its row in the table) against 0.514% to 1.355% for the other months of 2026, because the returns of the last shipments arrive after the data end. The tables show 0.682% overall by the credit date against 0.711% by the ship date, whose revenue leaves out the 439 lines that never ship.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="592" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
